# netsurf: a leaf element inserted between blocks is built alone in a line of its own (patch 407)
# Generated 2026-11-08
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 406)
#
# The census after 404-406 (r119, 97 full rebuilds): the largest local
# decline, "new element is not a plain block, list item or block of
# blocks" (10: claude 4, google 2, rte 2, guardian, oldreddit). A debug
# build (scratch only) logged the rejected elements: <img> (4), <textarea>
# (3), <input>, <iframe> -- each inserted BETWEEN block-level boxes of the
# parent (prev a block, next a block or a flex box) -- and a <div> holding
# a whole document (<html> inside, from innerHTML: stays full). Patch 378
# builds an <iframe>/<img> alone only when appended at the end, because
# box_build_element puts an inline-level box in a line at the END of the
# parent.
#
#  - html_rl_leaf_tag: iframe, img, input, textarea, button, select.
#  - html_rl_block_neighbour: the nearest boxed sibling on each side is a
#    block-level box directly in the parent (or none), with no text but
#    white space between (else it belongs in that text's line).
#  - html_rl_block_change: such a leaf, its children inline or controls
#    (a <select>'s options, a <button>'s text), is accepted (leafmid),
#    built alone; if built inline-level into the line at the end of the
#    parent it is moved into a NEW line right after its earlier block (the
#    old line freed if left empty; a following BOX_INLINE_END declines);
#    block-level, it takes the existing placement. The page is laid out
#    whole. Logged "a leaf element inserted between blocks, built alone"
#    and "leaf element placed in a line of its own".
#
